# The relevance gate (maintenance/evaluate-relevance.py) fingerprints the raw
# bytes of the catalog's runtime and data files, and of its own oracle inputs,
# and refuses to run when they drift. On a machine with core.autocrlf=true a
# plain checkout rewrites every one of those files to CRLF and changes the hash,
# so every text file in the plugin is pinned to LF on every platform.
#
# This file lives in the plugin, not only at the Pipelines repo root, because the
# plugin is published on its own and the root rule does not travel with it.
# After a deliberate change to a fingerprinted file, regenerate the fingerprints
# with maintenance/evaluate-relevance.py.
* text=auto eol=lf
